sequenceDiagram
  %% Option B of ADR 0248, for Nick's choice and not for building yet: the vpn Node lists the TLDs, the reserved names and the Routes outside any TLD, and sends each TLD to its Router; the Router holds that Cluster's Routes. It is the alternative to chart A and would take the same shared child name.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · shared step of Route, Node, Cluster and role kinds
  %% kind: dns.publish_delegated
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane R icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as VPN Node<br/>reached over ssh
  participant R as Router<br/>each Cluster
  Note over GW: Render all private DNS<br/>VPN state + one per Router
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - renders the VPN state: reserved names, TLD delegations and Routes outside any TLD
  %%> - renders one state per Router: the exact Routes of its Cluster
  %%> - takes one revision for the whole render, in the same transaction that reads the rows
  %%> - skips a Router whose stored digest equals its render
  GW->>SW: Start run with renders<br/>child workflow dns-publish
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the owning kind starts this step in its own run
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the VPN files, one file set per Router, and the revision
  SW->>R: Run the Router DNS phase<br/>ansible-playbook cluster-dns
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - installs `dnsmasq-base` and the unit when missing
  %%> - validates and writes the Cluster files, reloads or restarts, and asks its own address
  %%> Runs on:
  %%> - every Router whose digest changed, in parallel
  alt every Router answers
    %% path: routers-ready
    R-->>SW: Router DNS ready
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the Router address that answered the check names
    SW->>N: Run the VPN DNS phase<br/>ansible-playbook dns-publish
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - validates and installs `orbit.conf` with one `server=/TLD/ROUTER` line per delegated TLD
    %%> - skips an older revision, and reloads or restarts as in chart A
    Note over N: Check through the VPN DNS<br/>dig on the VPN address
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks the VPN DNS for the reserved names, a name outside any TLD and one name per delegated TLD
    %%> - the delegated name must come back from its Router
    alt VPN answers match
      %% path: succeeded
      N-->>SW: Phase result
      %%> Returns:
      %%> - the installed revision and the delegated TLDs
      SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
      %%> How the Gateway learns it:
      %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
      Note over GW: Record result
      %%> Result:
      %%> - the Router digests are stored after the checks pass
    else VPN write or check fails
      %% path: vpn-failed
      N--xSW: exit ≠ 0
      %%> When:
      %%> - dnsmasq refuses the files, or a delegated name does not come back from its Router
      SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
      Note over GW: Clear the Router digests
      %%> On the Node:
      %%> - the Routers keep their new state and the VPN Node keeps its last good files
      %%> - the cleared digests make the next publication write every Router again
    end
  else a Router write or check fails
    %% path: router-failed
    R--xSW: exit ≠ 0
    %%> When:
    %%> - SSH fails, the unit does not start or the Router does not answer its own names
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its error code
    Note over GW: Mark the owner failed
    %%> On the Node:
    %%> - the VPN Node is untouched, so the delegation of the failed Router stays as it was
    %%> - a Router written before the failure keeps its new state and its digest is cleared
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run the owning command again after fixing the cause
  end
